    {
      "id": "p0188-b003",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In the English script, a scientist named Al phys comes across as smart and professional when it comes to her work, but becomes shy, nerdy, and insecure when holding a casual conversation. The translator conveyed these qualities in Japanese by giving Al phys a mixture of casual speech patterns and polite speech patterns that fit her character. Alphys also uses the polite and somewhat feminine pronoun watashi when referring to herself.",
        "raw": "In the English script, a scientist named Al phys comes across as smart and\nprofessional when it comes to her work, but becomes shy, nerdy, and insecure\nwhen holding a casual conversation. The translator conveyed these qualities\nin Japanese by giving Al phys a mixture of casual speech patterns and\npolite speech patterns that fit her character. Alphys also uses the polite and\nsomewhat feminine pronoun watashi when referring to herself.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29179592,
          0.23560714,
          0.88636735,
          0.33968571
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.2897551,
          0.23489286,
          0.89842857,
          0.34075714
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          16,
          18,
          20,
          21,
          22,
          23
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "英文剧本中的科学家 Alphys 谈到工作时聪明而专业，闲聊时却害羞、宅气又不自信。译者把符合她性格的随意说法和礼貌说法混合起来，在日语中表现这些特点。Alphys 自称时还使用礼貌、略带女性色彩的代词 watashi（我）。",
        "status": "draft",
        "spans": [
          {
            "start": 102,
            "end": 109,
            "italic": true,
            "lang": "en"
          }
        ]
      },
